sequenceDiagram
  actor U as User
  box rgb(237,243,248) Controller API process
    participant H as HTTP handler
    participant O as OCC
    participant D as Selected Driver
  end
  participant P as PostgreSQL State
  participant S as Native storage

  Note over H,S: 1 · Admit and prepare
  U->>H: PATCH valid values or DELETE
  H->>O: Run mutation in transaction
  O->>O: Authorize the exact resource
  O->>P: Lock Namespace, then Configuration
  P-->>O: Locked ownership record
  O->>O: Check mutation rules under lock
  O->>D: Prepare exact update or delete
  D->>S: Capture original and storage identity
  S-->>D: Native document and identity
  D-->>O: Opaque receipt and observed identity
  O->>O: Check original and register undo

  Note over U,S: 2 · Apply and settle
  Note over O,P: Stage PATCH metadata before apply and DELETE metadata after apply
  O->>D: Apply once
  D->>S: Replace or delete only captured original
  S-->>D: Effect result or unknown response
  D-->>O: Apply result
  O-->>H: Mutation result
  H->>O: Append audit on success
  O->>P: Settle metadata and audit
  alt Commit acknowledged
    P-->>O: Commit confirmed
    O->>D: Dispose receipt
    O-->>H: Success
    H-->>U: PATCH 200 / DELETE 204
  else COMMIT outcome unknown
    P-->>O: Outcome unknown
    O->>D: Dispose receipt
    O-->>H: Unknown outcome
    H-->>U: Unknown outcome
    Note over O,S: No compensation or automatic replay
  else Known rollback
    P-->>O: Rollback known
    Note over U,S: 3 · Recheck ownership and restore conditionally
    O->>P: Begin fresh transaction and reacquire both locks in order
    P-->>O: Current record or unavailable
    alt Ownership missing, changed or unreadable
      Note over O,D: Stop before any restoration write
    else Original ownership confirmed
      O->>D: Settle or restore while both locks are held
      alt PATCH effect attributed
        D->>S: Replace only this operation's exact written document
        S-->>D: Restored, conflict or unresolved
      else DELETE effect attributed
        D->>S: Recreate original only if absent
        S-->>D: Restored, destination occupied or unresolved
      else Effect unapplied or attribution unproved
        Note over D,S: No restoration write
      end
      D-->>O: Internal disposition
    end
    O->>P: End fresh transaction and release locks
    O->>D: Dispose receipt
    O-->>H: Request failed
    H-->>U: Failure even after a proven restore
  end
